      "description": "Single-story 3-bedroom, 2-bathroom home in the Legend Point community of New Braunfels, TX 78130. Built in 2022, this 1,604-square-foot home backs directly to a greenbelt, so there are no rear neighbors and open green space beyond the back fence.\n\nThe single-level floor plan puts all three bedrooms, both full bathrooms, and the kitchen, dining, and living areas on one connected main floor — no stairs, easy to move through, and simple to maintain. Flooring runs carpet and vinyl throughout, a practical, low-upkeep choice for a near-new home. The layout keeps the living, dining, and kitchen areas open to each other, so the main living space stays bright and connected whether you're cooking, hosting, or relaxing.\n\nJust off the living area, a covered back patio overlooks the greenbelt — a shaded, private spot for morning coffee or weekend grilling. The privacy-fenced backyard offers room to garden, play, or add your own touches over time.\n\nAs a Legend Point resident, you get access to the community pool and playground, plus the wide, quiet streets the neighborhood is known for. The home sits down the street from Legend Point Elementary and Long Creek High School, with the middle school about five minutes away — a short drive on school mornings.\n\nQuick access to I-35 puts downtown New Braunfels about 10 minutes out and the Gruene Historic District about fifteen, where you'll find Gruene Hall, live music, restaurants, and local shops. New Braunfels is a place people plan vacations around — tube the Comal and Guadalupe Rivers, spend a day at Schlitterbahn Waterpark, explore Landa Park, or catch Wurstfest in the fall. Everyday needs are close too, with grocery stores, dining, and the growing south-side retail corridor just minutes away.\n\nNear-new 2022 construction, single-story living, low-maintenance finishes, and a greenbelt lot with no rear neighbors make this Legend Point home a strong option on the fast-growing south side of New Braunfels, TX.",
