      "description": "Central San Antonio location within Oak Park near Alamo Heights, the Broadway corridor, Brackenridge Park, The DoSeum, the San Antonio Zoo, Pearl, Downtown San Antonio, Fort Sam Houston, and the San Antonio International Airport, with quick access to I-410 and Hwy 281.\n\nPositioned on a 0.32-acre corner lot with mature oak trees, this 5-bedroom, 5-bath home combines updated systems, flexible living space, and proximity to major city destinations, restaurants, parks, museums, and employers.\n\nThe layout includes two living areas, separate dining room, main-level primary suite, main-level guest bedroom, and three additional upstairs bedrooms. Multiple living and bedroom configurations support guest accommodations, office space, workout rooms, hobby space, or multi-generational living. Interior features include engineered hardwood flooring, a Chef's Kitchen with natural stone countertops, custom cabinetry, gas cooking, pantry storage, built-ins, updated bathrooms, and Level 5 smooth wall texture throughout much of the home.\n\nOutdoor spaces include a covered patio, fenced backyard, landscaped yard, mature trees, and rear-entry attached 2-car garage. The lot provides usable outdoor space for entertaining, gardening, pets, or future outdoor additions.\n\nRecent updates completed by current ownership include a 2024 stone-coated steel tile roof, 2024 exterior stucco paint, 2024 gutters with leaf guards, 2023 dual HVAC systems, 2024 water heater, interior paint, updated hardware, painted fencing, repaired sprinkler system, refreshed landscaping, and epoxy-coated patio deck. Additional prior improvements include expanded covered patio areas, attic insulation, kitchen remodeling, and bathroom renovations.\n\nSmart home features include monitored Ring security system, Ring cameras, Ring video doorbell, smart lighting, smart locks, smart thermostat, network wiring, and Google Fiber availability. Several smart home devices and network equipment convey with the sale, along with the kitchen refrigerator.\n\nLocated within Alamo Heights ISD and zoned to Woodridge Elementary, Alamo Heights Middle School, and Alamo Heights High School. No HOA.",
